NAME
    enano - Enhanced Nano Launcher

SYNOPSIS
    enano [OPTIONS] [sudo] [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
    enano is a wrapper for the nano text editor that opens files in a new 
    gnome-terminal instance. It safely handles privilege escalation (sudo) 
    and supports opening multiple files simultaneously, preserving your 
    current terminal session.

    If no window-sizing options are passed, enano will read the default 
    behavior from the configuration file located at /etc/enano/settings.conf.

OPTIONS
    -f, --full-screen
        Opens the new gnome-terminal in full-screen mode.

    -m, --maximize
        Opens the new gnome-terminal in a maximized window.

    -n, --normal
        Opens the new gnome-terminal using the default window size.

    -h, --help
        Displays this help text and exits.

SPECIAL KEYWORDS
    sudo
        If 'sudo' is included before the file names, enano will prompt 
        for your password in the new terminal window and open the files 
        with root privileges.

EXAMPLES
    enano test.txt
        Opens test.txt in a new window using the default view from settings.conf.

    enano -f sudo /etc/hosts /etc/fstab
        Opens both /etc/hosts and /etc/fstab in a new, full-screen terminal 
        with root privileges.

    enano -m file1.js file2.js file3.js
        Opens three JavaScript files in a maximized terminal window.

FILES
    /etc/enano/settings.conf
        Configuration file. Use DEFAULT_VIEW to set base behavior 
        (e.g., DEFAULT_VIEW=-f).
        
    /etc/enano/help
        This documentation file.
